Package: rasblocking
Title: Scoring, Verification and Structural Diagnostics for Railroad Blocking Plans
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Annice", "Najafi", role = c("aut", "cre"),
                  email = "annicenajafi27@gmail.com")
Description: Tools for the railroad blocking problem as posed by the INFORMS RAS
    2026 Problem Solving Competition. Provides an exact reimplementation of the
    competition objective and its eleven feasibility checks, two independent
    verification gates that reject payloads which pass every feasibility check
    while misreporting their own cost, structural diagnostics that certify which
    demand is unservable by any feasible design, and the destination-pooling
    construction used to serve sub-tier demand. Reads any instance in the
    General Modeling Network Specification (GMNS) node/link format, so the
    diagnostics apply to networks beyond the competition instances. Depends on
    no mathematical programming solver and no Python.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.1)
Imports: data.table, jsonlite, igraph, stats, utils
Suggests: testthat (>= 3.0.0), shiny, bslib, DT, ggplot2
Config/testthat/edition: 3
